From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:07:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: reject source offsets on overlay planes

Overlay layers can't crop. KAPI only sends srcX/srcY for the main layer,
where they become the head's viewport point in, and NVKMS can't program a
source fetch offset. The offset of an overlay plane was silently dropped, so
a commit with a cropped overlay passed and showed the wrong part of the
framebuffer. Fail the commit, so that the compositor can fall back to
composition. Primary planes are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
index 243f8471..8ed23e92 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
@@ -1242,6 +1242,17 @@ plane_req_config_update(struct drm_plane *plane,
         return -EINVAL;
     }
 
+    /*
+     * Overlay layers can't crop: KAPI only sends srcX/srcY for the main layer,
+     * where they become the head's viewport point in, and NVKMS can't program
+     * a source fetch offset. Fail the commit instead of showing the wrong part
+     * of the framebuffer, so that the compositor can fall back to composition.
+     */
+    if (plane->type == DRM_PLANE_TYPE_OVERLAY &&
+        (plane_state->src_x != 0 || plane_state->src_y != 0)) {
+        return -EINVAL;
+    }
+
     /* Source values are 16.16 fixed point */
     req_config->config.srcX = plane_state->src_x >> 16;
     req_config->config.srcY = plane_state->src_y >> 16;
